WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.917
That sentence needs rescuing.

00:00:01.370 --> 00:00:03.823
Bile emulsifies fat into droplets.

00:00:04.114 --> 00:00:07.867
Lipase chemically digests it,
and bile is not an enzyme.

00:00:08.672 --> 00:00:12.805
Where are nutrients mainly absorbed,
and why is that surface efficient?

00:00:13.616 --> 00:00:14.640
Small intestine.

00:00:15.098 --> 00:00:18.991
Villi give a large surface area,
thin walls give a short crossing

00:00:18.991 --> 00:00:22.751
distance, and transport vessels
carry absorbed products away.

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:24.368
Last question.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:28.889
Why is a protein-rich food alone
not a complete balanced diet?

00:00:29.652 --> 00:00:33.381
We need suitable amounts from all
seven groups, including vitamins,

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.350
minerals, fiber, and water.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:39.973
Different nutrients have different jobs,
and foods usually contain mixtures.

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:41.316
Excellent.

00:00:41.595 --> 00:00:43.789
Our sandwich did not jump into the blood.

00:00:44.262 --> 00:00:48.117
Mechanical and chemical digestion
prepared its molecules, absorption

00:00:48.117 --> 00:00:50.138
moved them across, and cells used them.

00:00:50.497 --> 00:00:54.537
Clear processes, clear answers,
and no teacher tears required.
